      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-10-09T23:02:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can this library ever be used with more than one struct usb_i2c_config?  If not, document that in usb_i2c.h.\n\nIf this could be used with multiple struct usb_i2c_config, this static variable seems unsafe.  I would prefer either skip the optimization of saving this value, or making it per config somehow, e.g. by passing it around the stack or making it an indirect member of struct usb_i2c_config.  (Indirect because *config is const here, so a pointer to a non-cost size_t or containing struct would be needed.)",
      "revId": "dd1f72ee4d32fa4e8719c498eeb7c34eba4fb7af",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
