      "writtenOn": "2018-10-09T23:02:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this would be more readable as one line:\n\n  write_count \u003d ((peek[0] \u0026 0xf0) \u003c\u003c 4) | peek[2];\n\nOr since write_count is only used for expected_size:\n\n  /* 4 header bytes + the write count */\n  expected_size \u003d 4 + (((peek[0] \u0026 0xf0) \u003c\u003c 4) | peek[2]);\n\nOr if you prefer (hopefully result in same compiled code):\n\n  /* header bytes */\n  expected_size \u003d 4;\n  /* write count */\n  expected_size +\u003d ((peek[0] \u0026 0xf0) \u003c\u003c 4) | peek[2];",
      "range": {
